<content>
1: When the button "Export to francaisfacile" is clicked.
2: 
3: Depending on the quizName, the topic should be exported either to
4: francaisfacile.com , anglaisfacile.com, italienfacile.com, espagnolfacile.com or
5: allemandfacile.com
6: In types.ts, the QuizNames are on the very top.
7: 
8: When the button is clicked, a modal dialog should appear where the user has to select:
9: 1) The type of exercise. There is 1.1) Test à trous 1.2) Test avec des options et differents options pour
10: chaque question 1.3) Test avec des options et les mêmes options pour chaque trou
11: 
12: In the modal dialog, I want a group of radio buttons for these options, where you have to select exactly
13: one radio button.
14: 
15: When for example 1.1) Test à trous is selected, all the exercises from the database
16: for that topic and of type gapText , where there is only one gap with no options given, are fetched.
17: If 1.2) "Test avec des options differents" is selected, every exercise for the topic with type multiple
18: choice and every exercise of type gapText with exactly one gap and options given in the solution should be selected
19: If 1.3) "Test avec les mêmes options pour chaque exercice" is selected, then all the exercises from the database
20: of type gapText and of type multiple choice should be fetched. 
21: 
22: The chosen exercises should be displayed in a list in the modal dialog. Next to each exercise, there should be
23: a checkbox, so the exercise can be included in the export or not. At the top of the list,
24: there should be a Select All-Checkbox. 
25: Then all the selected exercises should be posted to the respective website (depending on the quizName). I think you need at least
26: 10 questions or exercises. If the user has selected less than 10, then the missing ones should be a copy
27: of the last one.
28: 
29: All the exercises for the topic should be fetched from the database
30: using the function getAllExercises and then filter these exercises for the topic.
31: 
32: 
33: The gap in my app is in curly braces, but when the exercise is submitted to francaisfacile, then
34: the gap must become a star and the response (which is inside my curly braces), must become the
35: response on francaisfacile.
36: 
37: Example:
38: My app: 
39: A week has {seven} days.
40: 
41: When posted to francaisfacile:
42: q = A week has * days
43: r = seven
44:     
45: where q is question and r = response
46: 
47: The upload of the images I have for each exercise needs to be done that way:
48: 
